# Consolidation workspace

When the task touches **pipeline review**, **SoR consolidation**, **validators**, **refactors**, or **railroad documentation** beyond live ops:

## Read first (mandatory)

1. [`consolidation/AGENTS.md`](../../consolidation/AGENTS.md)
2. [`consolidation/OBJECTIVE.md`](../../consolidation/OBJECTIVE.md)
3. [`consolidation/LIVE_SOURCES.md`](../../consolidation/LIVE_SOURCES.md)
4. [`consolidation/DECISIONS_PENDING.md`](../../consolidation/DECISIONS_PENDING.md)

Browse portal: [`consolidation/index.html`](../../consolidation/index.html)

## Golden rule

**Write only under `hart/consolidation/`** (including `consolidation/external/*` submodules). Do not edit live `jmri/`, `cats/`, `tables/`, `docs/wiring/`, live `wiki/`, or **`~/Desktop/HART/`**.

## Bench freeze (D12)

- **No Pi / layout host deploy** — no roster push, no `sync_hart_package.sh` from consolidation work
- **Desktop/HART is read-only** — inventory/audit only; slim/dedupe is a separate cutover project
- **Original live files stay untouched** until rebuild is verified and user starts cutover

## Validators

```bash
bash consolidation/validators/run_all.sh
```

Reports go to `consolidation/audits/`.

## Promotion

Cutover to live requires user approval + Tier A green + STATUS update. Live workflow stays frozen during consolidation.
